Description: A simple and unified evaluation toolkit for benchmarking single-cell
    and multiomics data simulation methods. Evaluates how realistic simulated data
    are compared to real biological datasets across three multiomics experimental
    designs: (i) paired multiomics (simultaneous co-assay from identical cells,
    e.g. 10x Chromium Multiome, SHARE-seq, SNARE-seq), which unlocks the full
    Category 6 multiomics integration and cross-modal alignment suite (joint-embedding
    Batch ASW, Cell-Type ASW, Graph Connectivity, Integration ARI, and Integration NMI);
    (ii) unpaired multiomics (independent scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq profiled from
    separate cells of the same tissue), supported through per-modality unimodal
    evaluation (Categories 1-5, 7, 8) and joint-embedding integration fidelity;
    and (iii) mosaic multiomics (partial co-measurement where only a subset of cells
    has both modalities, e.g. DOGMA-seq or mosaic pooling designs), handled by
    evaluating the paired and unimodal cell fractions across all 8 canonical
    categories. The toolkit quantifies simulation realism using 56
    evaluation measures organized into 8 canonical categories:
    (1) Distributional Properties: 10 univariate metrics (Wasserstein, KS, MAD,
    MAE, RMSE, Bhattacharyya, KDE-ISE, Runs statistic, NN mismatch,
    Inter-dataset silhouette) and 4 bivariate metrics (Fasano-Franceschini 2D
    KS, 2D EMD, 2D NN mismatch, 2D Inter-dataset silhouette) evaluated across 7
    cell-level, 7 feature-level, and 4 bivariate property pairs,
    (2) Sparsity & Zero-Inflation Dynamics: logistic dropout curve
    midpoint/slope/R2 (scRNA-seq), quadratic accessibility-sparsity curve
    RMSE/R2 (scATAC-seq), and posterior excess zero weight discrepancy,
    (3) Cellular Manifold & Clustering Concordance: MMD, Generative
    Precision/Recall, Silhouette ASW, Clustering Deviation Index (CDI),
    Neighborhood Purity, ARI, and NMI (with auxiliary Davies-Bouldin Index),
    (4) Technical Variation & Batch Mixing Dynamics: Batch Silhouette, PCR R2,
    CMS, Inverse Simpson Index (ISI), and Cross-Batch F1,
    (5) Biological Signal & Differential Fidelity: pseudobulk edgeR-QLF null
    P-value uniformity, accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and ROC-AUC
    across parallel scRNA-seq DE and scATAC-seq DA sub-categories,
    (6) Multiomics Integration & Alignment: joint-embedding Batch ASW,
    Cell-Type ASW, Graph Connectivity, Integration ARI, and Integration NMI,
    (7) Trajectory & Lineage Topology: HVG-filtered dynverse benchmark (Saelens
    et al., 2019) comprising HIM topology similarity, edge flip similarity,
    geodesic distance correlation, branch assignment F1, and Random Forest
    feature importance weighted correlation (wcor_features),
    (8) Computational Scalability & Efficiency: core-normalized execution
    runtime (core_seconds) and memory footprint per allocated core
    (memory_per_core_mib), with automated multi-core scaling and unified
    memory_mb resource benchmarking.
    Includes non-linear low-dimensional cell embedding projections (UMAP,
    t-SNE, PCA) with quantitative cluster separability (Silhouette) and fidelity
    (ARI) metrics, automated score normalization, leaderboards, 600 DPI bubble
    plots, and an interactive Shiny app studio.
